00:32:05.560 --> 00:32:08.880
Or, I don't even care what anyone thinks of me.

669
00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:14.100
I am an iconoclast, both of which are perfect for the smug Ryan.

670
00:32:15.540 --> 00:32:20.100
Because, by the way, it was in the script that he's wearing an untied bow tie.

671
00:32:20.260 --> 00:32:24.700
Like, this was a Mindy Kaling detail, and I totally noticed it, Mindy.

672
00:32:24.880 --> 00:32:28.960
I want to know where Mindy was when she saw someone that looked like that,

673
00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:31.060
and she was instantly, like, ticked off.

674
00:32:31.160 --> 00:32:32.240
Like, how dare you?

675
00:32:32.460 --> 00:32:34.240
Yeah, she was like, Ryan.

676
00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:41.020
Well, Randy Cordray told me that getting permission to use the Sesame Street characters

677
00:32:41.020 --> 00:32:42.260
was not easy.

678
00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:44.420
It was a very long process.

679
00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:46.120
I remember this, Jenna.

680
00:32:46.380 --> 00:32:49.860
I remember there was, like, scuttlebutt, like, what if we can't get it?

681
00:32:49.960 --> 00:32:51.760
They're, like, being kind of sticklers.

682
00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:57.280
Yeah, he said that it started off really easy, and Mindy confirmed this as well,

683
00:32:57.320 --> 00:33:00.620
that they had a conference call with the Children's Television Network,

684
00:33:00.620 --> 00:33:05.420
which is now called Sesame Street Workshop, asking if they could use Cookie Monster.

685
00:33:06.680 --> 00:33:09.860
And they had kind of shown them the outline of the script,

686
00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:12.280
and they were like, yes, you can.

687
00:33:12.500 --> 00:33:18.140
But Randy said it was with the caveat that we had to show them the final cut for final approval.

688
00:33:18.440 --> 00:33:20.060
But they said, go ahead and shoot it.

689
00:33:20.120 --> 00:33:21.140
We think it's going to be okay.

690
00:33:21.600 --> 00:33:27.020
Well, I guess after we shot it and showed it to them, they said no.

691
00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:29.140
Yeah, that's what I remember.

692
00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:29.720
Mm-hmm.

693
00:33:29.720 --> 00:33:34.100
So they set up another conference call with Greg Daniels, Paul Lieberstein,

694
00:33:34.720 --> 00:33:39.040
Steve Carell, and Randy Cordray with the senior executives

695
00:33:39.040 --> 00:33:42.000
at the New York headquarters of Sesame Workshop.

696
00:33:42.360 --> 00:33:43.060
Uh-oh.

697
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:47.500
Greg and Paul said, listen, this parody is really innocent.

698
00:33:47.500 --> 00:33:50.000
We are not making fun of Cookie Monster.

699
00:33:50.260 --> 00:33:52.700
We're making fun of Kevin's voice.

700
00:33:53.160 --> 00:33:54.860
So Randy was on the call.

701
00:33:55.080 --> 00:33:58.880
He said he could feel the executives softening to the idea.

702
00:33:58.880 --> 00:34:11.600
They're coming around, not quite there yet, until Steve Carell volunteered to appear on Sesame Street in the scene of their choosing.

703
00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:19.100
He said he would be in New York City soon, and he would do a cameo.

704
00:34:19.420 --> 00:34:21.060
Steve knows how to work it.

705
00:34:21.280 --> 00:34:24.760
And they were like, yes, I found his cameo.

706
00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:25.480
You did.

707
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:26.180
So we can play it.

708
00:34:26.220 --> 00:34:26.940
Oh, cute.

709
00:34:27.220 --> 00:34:27.400
Yes.

710
00:34:28.480 --> 00:34:29.260
Hi, I'm Steve.

711
00:34:29.580 --> 00:34:31.940
And I'm Abby and Elmo's Elmo.

712
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:34.720
And we're here to tell you all about the word vote.

713
00:34:35.080 --> 00:34:36.220
Yes, vote.

714
00:34:36.560 --> 00:34:36.680
Yes.

715
00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:38.720
Let's tell them what vote means.

716
00:34:38.860 --> 00:34:42.620
Well, the word vote means to make a choice between two or more things.

717
00:34:42.620 --> 00:34:45.580
And right now, we are going to show a vote.

718
00:34:45.780 --> 00:34:49.080
Oh, what is Elmo going to vote about, Mr. Steve?

719
00:34:49.260 --> 00:34:52.780
Well, we're going to vote to decide what we're going to have for snack time.

720
00:34:53.040 --> 00:34:53.520
Oh.

721
00:34:53.840 --> 00:34:54.680
This is exciting.

722
00:34:55.520 --> 00:34:56.760
Elmo can't wait to vote.

723
00:34:57.980 --> 00:34:58.780
That's adorable.

724
00:34:59.160 --> 00:35:00.080
It was so cute.

725
00:35:00.080 --> 00:35:01.080
I watched the whole thing.

726
00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:06.600
So they're going to vote on whether to have cheese or peanut butter and jelly as a snack.

727
00:35:06.820 --> 00:35:07.160
Okay.

728
00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:13.700
But then, very dramatically, there is a late-breaking third candidate for snack, and it's pizza.

729
00:35:13.880 --> 00:35:14.160
Oh, no.

730
00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:15.780
And pizza runs away with it.

731
00:35:16.080 --> 00:35:17.140
Pizza wins.

732
00:35:17.380 --> 00:35:19.160
But it's really cute.

733
00:35:19.240 --> 00:35:25.360
But that is why we were able to use Cookie Monster and The Count in our episode, because of Steve.

734
00:35:25.700 --> 00:35:27.720
Well, that is stinking cute.

735
00:35:28.480 --> 00:35:30.940
I love that Elmo calls him, Mrs. Steve.

736
00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:31.760
I know.

737
00:35:32.480 --> 00:35:35.060
Kevin is very upset by all of this.

738
00:35:35.240 --> 00:35:35.580
Yeah.

739
00:35:35.860 --> 00:35:36.180
Yeah.

740
00:35:36.180 --> 00:35:37.920
Everyone else is tickled.

741
00:35:38.300 --> 00:35:39.580
Dwight says, send me a link to that.

742
00:35:39.660 --> 00:35:40.760
And everyone's like, yeah, send me a link.

743
00:35:40.860 --> 00:35:41.400
Send me a link.

744
00:35:42.160 --> 00:35:46.100
Kevin appeals to Angela, who is beside herself happy.

745
00:35:46.300 --> 00:35:48.320
She says, this is my favorite day.

746
00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:52.260
And we got a fan question about it from Selena R.

747
00:35:52.420 --> 00:35:53.780
in Long Island, New York.

748
00:35:54.500 --> 00:35:59.720
In these later episodes, it seems like Angela becomes more emotional and humanized.

749
00:36:00.020 --> 00:36:01.040
Do you agree?

750
00:36:01.620 --> 00:36:04.400
If so, Angela, how did you interpret this?

751
00:36:04.400 --> 00:36:08.200
How did you feel about it, both now as a viewer and as an actor?

752
00:36:08.740 --> 00:36:12.840
In this episode especially, I felt like I saw so much growth in her character.

753
00:36:13.140 --> 00:36:17.220
I couldn't imagine Angela doing some of these scenes in the earlier episodes.

754
00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:19.620
Selena, I love this question.

755
00:36:19.620 --> 00:36:29.540
Because as a performer, my backstory for showing more emotion as Angela as the years went on is that she was very guarded in the beginning around the camera crew.

756
00:36:29.680 --> 00:36:31.280
She is a distrusting person.

757
00:36:31.280 --> 00:36:32.620
She doesn't like strangers.

758
00:36:32.920 --> 00:36:38.100
This would have been very awkward for her to have these people there every day.

759
00:36:38.100 --> 00:36:41.720
She, I'm sure, was very reluctant to participate.

760
00:36:42.340 --> 00:36:49.900
And so as the years grew and she became more comfortable, she just let her guard down a little bit more and showed more of her emotions.

761
00:36:50.660 --> 00:36:51.220
Right.

762
00:36:51.440 --> 00:36:53.840
So it's not like Angela is changing.

763
00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:58.160
It's just she's changing how much of herself she's revealing to this crew.

764
00:36:58.440 --> 00:36:59.000
Exactly.

765
00:36:59.560 --> 00:37:03.520
It's so funny because we never really talked about it.

766
00:37:03.720 --> 00:37:05.160
It just kind of happened.

767
00:37:05.480 --> 00:37:05.700
Yeah.

768
00:37:06.100 --> 00:37:06.480
Naturally.

769
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:06.980
Yeah.

770
00:37:07.140 --> 00:37:08.260
For all the characters.

771
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:09.840
Thank you for that question.

772
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:10.660
I thought that was great.

773
00:37:11.380 --> 00:37:14.940
Andy has a very exuberant talking head.

774
00:37:15.160 --> 00:37:16.240
He's super excited.

775
00:37:16.440 --> 00:37:17.720
It's Secretary's Day.

776
00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:19.280
He's made a banner.

777
00:37:20.020 --> 00:37:21.140
He's decorated.

778
00:37:21.700 --> 00:37:24.700
He said he's so excited for everyone to celebrate Erin.

779
00:37:24.980 --> 00:37:27.820
He really wanted everyone to know to celebrate her.

780
00:37:27.960 --> 00:37:28.560
Listen to what he did.

781
00:37:28.560 --> 00:37:34.300
He sent an email blast, a text blast, a good old-fashioned talk blast, and a snail mail blaSt.

782
00:37:34.860 --> 00:37:35.380
Yeah.

783
00:37:35.660 --> 00:37:40.480
Also in his talking head, he says if it weren't for secretaries, he wouldn't have a stepmom.

784
00:37:40.660 --> 00:37:43.860
Again, with Andy sharing random stuff from his paSt.

785
00:37:44.640 --> 00:37:48.980
We got a fan question slash catch from Anne O in Norway.

786
00:37:48.980 --> 00:37:49.860
Hi, Anne.

787
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:54.420
Andy says he has a stepmom, but later his parents are still married.

788
00:37:54.420 --> 00:37:55.340
What's going on?

789
00:37:55.760 --> 00:37:56.660
Welcome, Anne.

790
00:37:56.660 --> 00:38:00.420
Welcome to the mystery of Andy's backstory.

791
00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:01.760
It's true.

792
00:38:01.760 --> 00:38:06.020
I had to say Anne's catch because I think we were all thinking it.

793
00:38:06.180 --> 00:38:06.400
Yeah.

794
00:38:07.020 --> 00:38:08.520
Well, another thing's happening today.

795
00:38:08.660 --> 00:38:09.480
Pam is back.

796
00:38:09.680 --> 00:38:11.360
She's back from her maternity leave.

797
00:38:11.740 --> 00:38:14.640
She is going to put a photo on her desk of Cece.

798
00:38:15.040 --> 00:38:18.140
At two minutes, that was a photo of my real niece, Cece.

799
00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:19.340
Aw, cute.

800
00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:21.800
She's also going to notice that her plant died.

801
00:38:22.440 --> 00:38:24.220
Jim said he didn't even know it existed.

802
00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:27.720
That made me laugh because I feel like my husband would do that.

803
00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:28.880
I have all of these plants.

804
00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:31.940
Whenever I travel for work, I'm like, okay, two things.

805
00:38:32.760 --> 00:38:35.460
Change out my hummingbird feeders and my plants.

806
00:38:35.940 --> 00:38:38.400
I always am not sure what I'm going to get when I come home.

807
00:38:38.680 --> 00:38:40.500
Well, Dwight said he chose to let it die.

808
00:38:40.960 --> 00:38:42.080
Welcome back, Pam.

809
00:38:43.420 --> 00:38:45.140
Fan question from Caitlin C.

810
00:38:45.220 --> 00:38:45.720
in Iowa.

811
00:38:46.500 --> 00:38:50.060
Is this proof that Pam was buying all the plants for the front desk?

812
00:38:50.300 --> 00:38:51.960
Oh, I like to think that.

813
00:38:52.160 --> 00:38:52.700
I do too.

814
00:38:53.060 --> 00:38:54.480
Well, there was more to the scene.

815
00:38:54.840 --> 00:38:58.420
At 25 seconds, what would have happened, it was a deleted scene,

816
00:38:59.020 --> 00:39:04.080
is that Pam would find a very old box of cupcakes.

817
00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:09.220
That was a gift, like a baby gift, that was left on her desk for weeks.

818
00:39:09.220 --> 00:39:14.280
It was covered in fruit flies, and she had one of her drawers that was full of maggots.

819
00:39:14.440 --> 00:39:15.280
My gosh.

820
00:39:15.560 --> 00:39:15.880
Mm-hmm.

821
00:39:16.340 --> 00:39:20.320
Pam's dialogue would have been, ugh, who left cupcakes on my desk for six weeks?

822
00:39:20.540 --> 00:39:22.560
My drawer is filled with maggots.

823
00:39:22.700 --> 00:39:27.140
To which Dwight jumps up, runs over to the drawer protectively, and says,

824
00:39:27.300 --> 00:39:28.100
those are mine.

825
00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:30.600
I was breeding maggots for personal use.

826
00:39:30.840 --> 00:39:32.700
I have nothing to do with the fruit flies, though.

827
00:39:33.360 --> 00:39:34.560
Did we shoot that?

828
00:39:34.780 --> 00:39:35.220
Yes.

829
00:39:35.380 --> 00:39:36.560
I have no memory of that.

830
00:39:36.640 --> 00:39:37.840
It's in deleted scenes.

831
00:39:37.840 --> 00:39:38.800
That's crazy to me.

832
00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:42.740
It's crazy, but this is what was happening on Pam's desk while she was away.

833
00:39:42.980 --> 00:39:43.840
Her plants were dying.

834
00:39:43.960 --> 00:39:46.120
There were fruit flies and maggots in her drawer.

835
00:39:46.700 --> 00:39:52.020
Randy did share, for this deleted scene, we used Bob Dunn's animal rentals for flies and maggots.

836
00:39:52.600 --> 00:39:54.900
Trainers were Megan Frazier and Kevin Kinzer.

837
00:39:55.420 --> 00:40:01.420
So now, Andy is really going to do everything he can to have Aaron have this great Secretary's Day,

838
00:40:01.460 --> 00:40:04.580
and that starts with going to Michael and asking Michael,

839
00:40:04.580 --> 00:40:05.820
what do you have planned?

840
00:40:05.820 --> 00:40:07.100
What are you going to do for her?

841
00:40:07.800 --> 00:40:11.460
And Michael says he's going to give her $15.

842
00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:15.820
To which Andy says, I think maybe step it up.

843
00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:17.480
Like, why don't you take her to lunch?

844
00:40:17.980 --> 00:40:20.760
Oh, Michael does not want to spend a lunch with Aaron.

845
00:40:20.920 --> 00:40:21.280
Oh, no.

846
00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:23.660
It's like Andy said, I think you should get a root canal.

847
00:40:24.240 --> 00:40:25.320
It's so true.

848
00:40:25.500 --> 00:40:26.360
Michael's expression.

849
00:40:26.680 --> 00:40:30.660
Well, this scene was bigger, and it explained the whole $15 thing.

850
00:40:30.660 --> 00:40:33.220
Yeah, that was a very specific amount of money.

851
00:40:33.560 --> 00:40:39.580
While it's in deleted scenes, Michael explains the $15, and it leads into a Pam talking head.

852
00:40:39.720 --> 00:40:40.720
I think we should hear it.

853
00:40:41.440 --> 00:40:44.300
I was just wondering what you had planned for Secretary's Day.

854
00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:46.240
Oh, I'm going to give Aaron $15.

855
00:40:47.340 --> 00:40:47.740
Wow.

856
00:40:48.420 --> 00:40:48.820
Why?

857
00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:51.080
Because that's what I always used to do with Pam.

858
00:40:51.660 --> 00:40:57.520
See, Pam decided that she would rather have the cash value of her half of lunch were I to take her out.

859
00:40:57.520 --> 00:41:02.760
So, she promises every year to take that money, go to Cooper's, and buy herself a sundae.

860
00:41:03.020 --> 00:41:03.500
Yeah.

861
00:41:04.120 --> 00:41:05.700
I can't believe that worked.

862
00:41:09.420 --> 00:41:10.420
That's pretty great.

863
00:41:10.640 --> 00:41:11.180
I know.

864
00:41:11.280 --> 00:41:11.800
I loved it.

865
00:41:12.420 --> 00:41:15.000
Well, I have a background catch for this scene.

866
00:41:15.820 --> 00:41:22.200
You know, earlier at reception, one of the gifts that Aaron got for Secretary's Day was like a little stuffed dog.

867
00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:22.800
Did you notice?

868
00:41:23.280 --> 00:41:23.960
Oh, yeah.

869
00:41:23.960 --> 00:41:33.720
Well, at 2 minutes and 33 seconds, in the background, through the window, I think Aaron is, like, pretending to give her stuffed dog a drink of water.

870
00:41:34.080 --> 00:41:34.740
Oh, no way.

871
00:41:34.740 --> 00:41:35.320
From a cup.

872
00:41:35.560 --> 00:41:37.140
And then it's talking on the phone.

873
00:41:37.340 --> 00:41:37.460
Right.

874
00:41:37.460 --> 00:41:40.940
She's doing all this business with her little stuffed dog.

875
00:41:41.100 --> 00:41:43.260
Well, Andy taped the phone to its head.

876
00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:44.580
Earlier, yes.

877
00:41:44.580 --> 00:41:44.780
Earlier.

878
00:41:44.980 --> 00:41:48.080
And then she waves the dog's paw at Michael.

879
00:41:48.300 --> 00:41:48.660
Mm-hmm.

880
00:41:49.280 --> 00:41:49.660
Yeah.

881
00:41:49.920 --> 00:41:51.700
Because she really is loving that stuffed animal.

882
00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:57.080
Well, on a rewatch, you can watch the stuffed dog show through the window during this scene.

883
00:41:57.260 --> 00:41:58.380
I need to see it.

884
00:41:58.740 --> 00:42:02.780
Michael is persuaded by Andy, and he's going to invite Aaron to lunch.

885
00:42:02.960 --> 00:42:04.400
She suggests Hayworth's.

886
00:42:04.820 --> 00:42:08.020
And Michael's like, oh, he's not feeling it.

887
00:42:08.160 --> 00:42:09.740
But ultimately, that's where they go.

888
00:42:09.960 --> 00:42:12.280
I could not find a real Hayworth's in Scranton.

889
00:42:12.360 --> 00:42:12.740
Same.

890
00:42:13.060 --> 00:42:13.680
Looked it up.

891
00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:14.340
Couldn't find it.

892
00:42:14.340 --> 00:42:19.160
I did find a great article on mental floss that gives you a Dunder Mifflin tour of Scranton

893
00:42:19.160 --> 00:42:21.780
of all the places that actually exist and that you can go.

894
00:42:21.940 --> 00:42:23.360
I found that same thing, too.

895
00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:25.660
And Hayworth's is not on the liSt.

896
00:42:26.220 --> 00:42:27.400
Two ladies that Google.

897
00:42:27.720 --> 00:42:28.920
Look at us go.

898
00:42:29.160 --> 00:42:30.720
Googling the same things.

899
00:42:31.480 --> 00:42:33.660
I have a few catches in this scene.

900
00:42:33.840 --> 00:42:34.620
Ooh, let's hear it.

901
00:42:34.920 --> 00:42:39.220
At three minutes and one second, when Michael is approaching Aaron's desk, the front door

902
00:42:39.220 --> 00:42:39.820
is closed.

903
00:42:40.320 --> 00:42:40.800
Okay.

904
00:42:40.800 --> 00:42:44.840
But at three minutes and nine seconds, the front door is open.

905
00:42:46.140 --> 00:42:47.360
Continuity catch, folks.

906
00:42:47.620 --> 00:42:48.140
Ding, ding, ding.

907
00:42:48.560 --> 00:42:54.640
Also, through that door, there is a picture on the wall that I have personally never noticed

908
00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:54.960
before.

909
00:42:55.300 --> 00:42:58.700
It's some sort of, I don't know what, mountainy or something.

910
00:42:58.860 --> 00:43:00.000
It's hazy in the background.

911
00:43:00.720 --> 00:43:02.420
Did we always have a picture there?

912
00:43:02.840 --> 00:43:04.560
Why is this the first time I'm seeing it?

913
00:43:04.600 --> 00:43:05.480
I don't know.

914
00:43:06.020 --> 00:43:08.180
But here is the major catch from the scene.

915
00:43:08.280 --> 00:43:09.700
And this is truly major.

916
00:43:09.700 --> 00:43:14.460
And it is, in fact, also a fan mail flurry.

917
00:43:18.110 --> 00:43:20.170
It's a fan mail flurry.

918
00:43:23.460 --> 00:43:25.380
I love my new sting.

919
00:43:26.180 --> 00:43:30.160
At three minutes and four seconds, Anna H.

920
00:43:30.300 --> 00:43:31.960
from Columbus, Ohio, Rudy D.

921
00:43:32.120 --> 00:43:33.140
from Utah, and

922
00:43:33.140 --> 00:43:33.860
Amanda H.

923
00:43:33.940 --> 00:43:40.460
from Boston, and many more, all said, Aaron is wearing purple flower earrings in

924
00:43:40.460 --> 00:43:41.140
this episode.

925
00:43:41.140 --> 00:43:46.060
Are they the same earrings that Pam wore in New York for art school?

926
00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:46.720
What?

927
00:43:47.680 --> 00:43:49.960
Yes, they are, folks.

928
00:43:50.180 --> 00:43:55.360
They recycled Pam's art school earrings, and they put them on Aaron for Secretary's Day.

929
00:43:55.600 --> 00:43:57.300
I took a side-by-side screenshot.

930
00:43:57.820 --> 00:44:02.360
These are the earrings that Pam was wearing in the hallway in Weight Loss Part 2.

931
00:44:02.360 --> 00:44:04.840
What a fantastic catch.

932
00:44:05.860 --> 00:44:07.260
I'm applauding it.

933
00:44:07.380 --> 00:44:08.440
Super well done.

934
00:44:08.620 --> 00:44:09.600
I'm going to show you the pick.

935
00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:10.540
I want to see the pick.

936
00:44:12.180 --> 00:44:13.540
Oh, my gosh.

937
00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:14.780
Exactly the same.

938
00:44:15.020 --> 00:44:15.200
Yep.

939
00:44:15.660 --> 00:44:16.740
What's going to happen next?

940
00:44:16.740 --> 00:44:18.160
She's going to wear Meredith's vest?

941
00:44:18.420 --> 00:44:19.140
What's happening?

942
00:44:19.420 --> 00:44:20.180
Oh, my gosh.

943
00:44:20.180 --> 00:44:23.840
I would love for Aaron to wear Meredith's veSt.

944
00:44:24.340 --> 00:44:25.440
That would be incredible.

945
00:44:25.880 --> 00:44:31.340
In the kitchen, there's some people enjoying Kevin's cookie monster bit.

946
00:44:31.500 --> 00:44:32.900
It would be Meredith and Daryl.

947
00:44:33.420 --> 00:44:34.740
They have cookies out.

948
00:44:34.900 --> 00:44:36.300
They tempt him to have one.

949
00:44:36.440 --> 00:44:38.380
So then Daryl can just go, nom, nom, nom, nom, nom.

950
00:44:38.760 --> 00:44:39.280
Yes.

951
00:44:39.600 --> 00:44:45.100
Kevin is starting to clue in that maybe they're not making fun of cookie monster.

952
00:44:45.340 --> 00:44:46.480
Maybe they're making fun of him.

953
00:44:46.740 --> 00:44:48.740
At first, he doesn't want to eat the cookie.

954
00:44:48.740 --> 00:44:49.740
He is suspicious.

955
00:44:50.020 --> 00:44:54.420
He says, you just brought those cookies so that I'll eat one and you can make fun of me.

956
00:44:54.480 --> 00:44:57.600
And Daryl's like, I brought these cookies because it's my birthday.

957
00:44:58.020 --> 00:45:00.400
Fan question from Timber Bee in Tennessee.

958
00:45:00.840 --> 00:45:01.620
Hold on.

959
00:45:01.760 --> 00:45:05.180
It's Secretary's Day, but it's also Daryl's birthday?

960
00:45:05.520 --> 00:45:08.140
Why didn't the PPC throw him a birthday party?

961
00:45:08.860 --> 00:45:09.900
Poor Daryl.

962
00:45:10.360 --> 00:45:12.000
No birthday cake for him.

963
00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:13.320
He needs a Fudgie the Whale.

964
00:45:13.740 --> 00:45:15.460
I don't think it was his birthday.

965
00:45:15.980 --> 00:45:16.500
Same.

966
00:45:16.500 --> 00:45:20.680
I think he was just making it up to make Kevin eat the cookie.

967
00:45:21.480 --> 00:45:23.200
Kevin is going to go to Gabe.

968
00:45:23.540 --> 00:45:24.980
He's going to show Gabe the video.

969
00:45:25.280 --> 00:45:28.920
I think he wants to know, are they making fun of me?

970
00:45:28.960 --> 00:45:29.700
Is this appropriate?

971
00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:31.880
And Gabe is not having it.

972
00:45:32.480 --> 00:45:34.920
Oh, Gabe lights up.

973
00:45:35.060 --> 00:45:36.520
He's finally got his cause.

974
00:45:36.820 --> 00:45:39.980
Something that will demand respect from the coworkers.

975
00:45:40.200 --> 00:45:42.320
His talking head is hilarious to me.

976
00:45:42.320 --> 00:45:46.040
He said that his beginning there has been a little bit of a fiasco.

977
00:45:46.320 --> 00:45:49.420
I loved it when he said some of them still think I'm the IT guy.

978
00:45:49.640 --> 00:45:51.020
That just cracked me up.

979
00:45:51.160 --> 00:45:55.580
I mean, some of them probably Creed and Meredith have not paid attention.

980
00:45:55.960 --> 00:45:58.460
But the cookie monster thing is Gabe's opportunity.

981
00:45:58.460 --> 00:46:01.720
He's really going to show them that he's the authority figure.

982
00:46:01.960 --> 00:46:03.640
And this starts a whole storyline.

983
00:46:04.140 --> 00:46:07.220
Well, lady, we got a fan question from KCA in Canada.

984
00:46:07.220 --> 00:46:11.480
Am I the only one who thinks everybody is being too mean to Kevin?

985
00:46:12.120 --> 00:46:15.740
Maybe I'm just too sensitive and I've seen the episode too many times.

986
00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:20.000
But re-watching it now, it feels genuinely kind of mean.

987
00:46:20.560 --> 00:46:21.140
Thoughts?

988
00:46:21.860 --> 00:46:28.840
Casey, I'm glad you wrote in because I also kind of thought, like, Gabe is right.

989
00:46:29.080 --> 00:46:30.300
He should shut this down.

990
00:46:30.300 --> 00:46:34.780
This is, like, not cool to do to your coworker.

991
00:46:35.520 --> 00:46:36.520
I'm with you.

992
00:46:36.520 --> 00:46:37.580
So I'm with you too.

993
00:46:37.580 --> 00:46:39.840
I think it went across the line.

994
00:46:40.520 --> 00:46:42.000
But I will say this.

995
00:46:42.380 --> 00:46:46.100
I imagine everyone in that office hits their breaking point with Kevin.

996
00:46:46.300 --> 00:46:51.300
I mean, he did walk up to Pam and pretend to be a baby crying to see if her boobs would produce milk.

997
00:46:51.620 --> 00:46:52.060
Yes.

998
00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:56.580
So probably there is part of them that just delighted in it for a little bit.

999
00:46:56.720 --> 00:46:57.740
But I think they went too far.

1000
00:46:58.280 --> 00:46:58.540
Yeah.

1001
00:46:58.740 --> 00:47:03.800
Well, I totally get why the characters at Dunder Mifflin would delight in this parody video.

1002
00:47:04.080 --> 00:47:06.180
But at the same time, Casey, I'm with you.

1003
00:47:06.520 --> 00:47:07.620
Yeah, I see it.

1004
00:47:08.020 --> 00:47:09.540
Well, Gabe is going to address the bullpen.

1005
00:47:09.840 --> 00:47:15.740
He's going to tell them that he forbids anyone from discussing or sharing the parody video.

1006
00:47:15.880 --> 00:47:17.420
And that is coming from corporate.

1007
00:47:17.620 --> 00:47:18.700
So they better listen to it.

1008
00:47:18.880 --> 00:47:19.300
Mm-hmm.

1009
00:47:20.040 --> 00:47:22.560
It doesn't seem like anyone's going to listen to it.

1010
00:47:22.560 --> 00:47:23.380
It really doesn't.

1011
00:47:23.900 --> 00:47:28.920
Well, now we are in the car on the way to Aaron's Secretary's Day lunch.

1012
00:47:29.160 --> 00:47:30.140
Michael is driving.

1013
00:47:30.520 --> 00:47:32.180
He would rather not talk.

1014
00:47:32.640 --> 00:47:41.760
He's hoping that he could listen to his audiobook, which is a novelization of the movie Precious based on the novel Push by Sapphire.

1015
00:47:41.760 --> 00:47:49.260
Per Randy Cordray, all of these driving scenes were filmed on Burbank Boulevard near Balboa Park, which was our go-to street.

1016
00:47:49.420 --> 00:47:50.900
There's no palm trees on this street.

1017
00:47:51.140 --> 00:48:00.820
I love that it was someone's job to drive around the vicinity of where we shoot looking for stretches of road with no palm trees.

1018
00:48:00.820 --> 00:48:01.720
Like, that was their job.

1019
00:48:01.840 --> 00:48:03.860
They're like, go find me a street with no palm trees.

1020
00:48:04.100 --> 00:48:05.420
This was the main one.

1021
00:48:05.740 --> 00:48:08.880
As I watched the scene, I looked for palm trees.

1022
00:48:08.880 --> 00:48:09.700
There weren't any.

1023
00:48:09.820 --> 00:48:11.700
But I did see the mountains in the background.

1024
00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:12.580
Mm-hmm.

1025
00:48:12.680 --> 00:48:12.900
Yeah.

1026
00:48:13.120 --> 00:48:16.060
I mean, you're not going to find no mountains and no palm trees.

1027
00:48:16.280 --> 00:48:16.540
I know.

1028
00:48:16.920 --> 00:48:18.500
We just went with no palm trees.

1029
00:48:19.180 --> 00:48:21.320
Steve was not actually driving in the scene.

1030
00:48:21.480 --> 00:48:24.840
The car was being towed behind one of those camera insert cars.

1031
00:48:25.420 --> 00:48:30.220
And Randy shared that we used lipstick cameras that were suction cupped to the windshield.

1032
00:48:30.820 --> 00:48:32.020
That's how we shot it.

1033
00:48:32.960 --> 00:48:36.320
Randy also shared that lipstick cameras were often problematic.

1034
00:48:36.320 --> 00:48:41.180
And whenever we could have a camera operator in a vehicle with us, that was preferred.

1035
00:48:41.560 --> 00:48:46.220
But if you wanted to get people from the front, you had to use these lipstick cameras.

1036
00:48:46.440 --> 00:48:52.440
But he said we had a special camera technician named Tim Arashaban, I hope I'm saying your last name right,

1037
00:48:52.640 --> 00:48:55.840
who was an absolute master of these lipstick cameras.

1038
00:48:55.840 --> 00:48:58.920
And we actually rarely had problems, thanks to Tim.

1039
00:48:59.120 --> 00:48:59.860
So thank you, Tim.

1040
00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:00.600
Thank you, Tim.

1041
00:49:00.820 --> 00:49:02.560
We used those lipstick cameras a lot.

1042
00:49:02.640 --> 00:49:02.940
We did.

1043
00:49:03.460 --> 00:49:07.000
So there's a lot of this scene in the deleted scenes on the DVD.

1044
00:49:07.660 --> 00:49:09.660
Guess who narrates the book?

1045
00:49:10.300 --> 00:49:11.520
Oh, I know this.

1046
00:49:11.820 --> 00:49:12.880
I know this.

1047
00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:18.540
In the script, they had a suggestion of someone, but that is not who narrated it when we filmed.

1048
00:49:18.820 --> 00:49:19.120
Okay.

1049
00:49:19.120 --> 00:49:20.940
I know who they put in the script.

1050
00:49:21.160 --> 00:49:22.380
It was David Hyde Pierce.

1051
00:49:23.100 --> 00:49:23.500
Exactly.

1052
00:49:23.880 --> 00:49:25.200
Who ended up doing it?

1053
00:49:25.400 --> 00:49:26.940
Our editor, Dave Rogers.

1054
00:49:27.340 --> 00:49:28.720
Oh my gosh, that's perfect.

1055
00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:29.740
I love it.

1056
00:49:30.180 --> 00:49:31.820
It was fun to hear his voice.

1057
00:49:31.820 --> 00:49:41.180
The other thing I loved about the deleted scenes for this is that Erin has a talking head where she explains how she is coming up with conversation topics.

1058
00:49:41.180 --> 00:49:43.040
So she has things to talk about.

1059
00:49:43.520 --> 00:49:44.400
Let's hear it.

1060
00:49:44.780 --> 00:49:48.240
I really want to impress Michael, and I don't want to take any chances.

1061
00:49:48.240 --> 00:49:58.880
So I went to a website that listed hundreds of interesting conversation starters, and I'll just break them out whenever there's a pause or even maybe if there's not,

1062
00:49:58.900 --> 00:50:04.800
because bosses like women who can talk at length on things.

1063
00:50:04.800 --> 00:50:18.140
So that would have played before the car scene, and while she's searching on this website for these talking points, all of these advertisements keep popping up, these pop-up ads,

1064
00:50:18.260 --> 00:50:21.300
and she's having a hard time clicking on her article.

1065
00:50:21.980 --> 00:50:24.060
It's just a funny background detail.

1066
00:50:24.320 --> 00:50:25.980
It's at 2 minutes, 25 seconds.

1067
00:50:26.440 --> 00:50:30.360
Randy shared with us that all of the motion graphics were created by Henry Sane.

1068
00:50:30.740 --> 00:50:31.100
Wow.

1069
00:50:31.700 --> 00:50:35.600
Well, you're going to see a few of these conversation starters coming up in the car.

1070
00:50:36.040 --> 00:50:38.540
Erin says, so what decade would you have chosen to be a teenager?

1071
00:50:39.240 --> 00:50:44.800
And then we're going to get to the restaurant for a very awkward lunch, and Erin is going to hit them with this.

1072
00:50:44.980 --> 00:50:46.620
Do you have a favorite age or month?

1073
00:50:47.740 --> 00:50:49.780
Michael does not know what to do with this.

1074
00:50:49.940 --> 00:50:52.680
She goes on to say, how many pillows do you sleep on at night?

1075
00:50:53.580 --> 00:50:58.700
Well, you know, in the script, Michael had a response to that that got cut out in editing.

1076
00:50:58.940 --> 00:50:59.900
Oh, what'd he say?

1077
00:50:59.900 --> 00:51:02.400
Michael says, none, just my body pillow.

1078
00:51:03.400 --> 00:51:05.980
And then he changes the subject to Andy.

1079
00:51:06.320 --> 00:51:08.740
But that line did not make it in the final cut.

1080
00:51:08.740 --> 00:51:10.080
But I think that's very funny.

1081
00:51:10.200 --> 00:51:14.340
I just imagine Michael always sleeping on that little bench at the end of his bed.

1082
00:51:14.480 --> 00:51:17.820
It's hard to picture him in the actual bed after that scene.

1083
00:51:17.920 --> 00:51:18.180
I know.

1084
00:51:18.400 --> 00:51:18.820
At dinner party.

1085
00:51:19.220 --> 00:51:23.600
Well, Erin is going to continue to overshare, if you will, at this lunch.

1086
00:51:23.760 --> 00:51:24.840
She's just talking and talking.

1087
00:51:24.960 --> 00:51:25.620
She can't stop.

1088
00:51:25.620 --> 00:51:31.540
Yeah, she says she used to work at a Taco Bell Express, but she couldn't hack it when it became a full Taco Bell.

1089
00:51:31.780 --> 00:51:32.960
It was just too stressful.

1090
00:51:33.620 --> 00:51:36.300
We had a fan question from Beth W.

1091
00:51:36.360 --> 00:51:41.160
in New York City who loves that line, wants to know who wrote that amazing joke.

1092
00:51:41.700 --> 00:51:48.340
Mindy Kaling said that Danny Chun wrote the Taco Bell Express line, and it's one of her favorites in the episode.

1093
00:51:49.120 --> 00:51:56.040
I looked it up, the difference between a Taco Bell Express and a Taco Bell, and I see why it might be more stressful for Erin.

1094
00:51:56.540 --> 00:51:59.980
Taco Bell Express, if my memory is correct, there's no seating area.

1095
00:52:00.320 --> 00:52:00.680
No.

1096
00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:03.860
It is to serve, quote, hungry customers on the go.

1097
00:52:04.160 --> 00:52:07.240
It's a grab-and-go, and it also has a smaller menu.

1098
00:52:07.240 --> 00:52:09.280
It's just the tacos and burritos.

1099
00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:21.640
And so, yeah, if you went from grab-and-go to a seated restaurant, when I worked in fast food, I have to say, like, 50% of it is just cleaning up that dining room.

1100
00:52:21.780 --> 00:52:22.560
I bet.

1101
00:52:22.840 --> 00:52:23.180
You know?

1102
00:52:23.380 --> 00:52:24.380
People are messy.

1103
00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:25.860
People are messy.

1104
00:52:26.160 --> 00:52:32.900
You know, the trash cans say thank you, and I used to say, you know, that's for you, the gueSt.

1105
00:52:33.440 --> 00:52:36.600
They're not thanking me, the employee, for throwing your stuff away.

1106
00:52:36.880 --> 00:52:38.000
They're thanking you.

1107
00:52:38.240 --> 00:52:41.140
That's what, carry your stuff over and throw it out on your way out.

1108
00:52:41.280 --> 00:52:48.380
Maybe trash cans should have a longer message, like, thank you for not being a total a-hole and putting your trash where you're supposed to put it.

1109
00:52:48.460 --> 00:52:50.860
It's literally on your way out of the restaurant.

1110
00:52:51.060 --> 00:52:53.100
You have to pass by it anyway.

1111
00:52:53.740 --> 00:52:54.880
Clean up after yourselves.

1112
00:52:55.060 --> 00:52:56.560
If you make the mess, clean it up.

1113
00:52:56.660 --> 00:52:58.000
My gosh, how hard is that?

1114
00:52:59.340 --> 00:52:59.780
Ah.

1115
00:53:02.080 --> 00:53:03.720
I don't even know where we are now.

1116
00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:04.680
I do, I do.

1117
00:53:04.980 --> 00:53:10.520
Okay, so this scene, Jenna, was even bigger, of Erin just talking and talking.

1118
00:53:11.660 --> 00:53:14.620
There was part of it that just really cracked me up.

1119
00:53:14.620 --> 00:53:15.880
It's in deleted scenes.

1120
00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:19.220
It's about what's in her purse.

1121
00:53:19.220 --> 00:53:20.200
You have to hear it.

1122
00:53:20.940 --> 00:53:22.620
In my foster home, I never had a desk.

1123
00:53:22.860 --> 00:53:25.980
So it's like a, I don't mean that I didn't like my foster home.

1124
00:53:26.140 --> 00:53:26.880
I did like it.

1125
00:53:26.880 --> 00:53:29.300
I just didn't have a desk there, so, sorry.

1126
00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:30.700
I know, I feel weird.

1127
00:53:30.820 --> 00:53:35.400
I think I'm nervous and you're looking at me like I'm weird, but my blood sugar is really low.

1128
00:53:35.640 --> 00:53:37.380
You know, I didn't have my Luna Bar this morning.

1129
00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:38.900
I thought I'd put my Luna Bar in my purse.

1130
00:53:39.400 --> 00:53:41.840
But it turns out I put my TV remote instead.

1131
00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:43.280
You ever, see?

1132
00:53:45.980 --> 00:53:48.000
There's no, there's no woman nutrition.

1133
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:49.160
Did you want me to take that, or?

1134
00:53:49.880 --> 00:53:51.300
Oh, I just wanted you to know it was real.

1135
00:53:51.440 --> 00:53:52.600
Oh, okay.

1136
00:53:54.160 --> 00:53:55.920
No folic acid in that, though.

1137
00:53:55.920 --> 00:53:58.560
Can you imagine eating your TV remote for breakfast?

1138
00:53:58.940 --> 00:54:02.260
I don't know if it would kill you, but it wouldn't even taste good to begin with.

1139
00:54:02.560 --> 00:54:03.620
But I don't know.

1140
00:54:04.160 --> 00:54:07.440
There's so many things that are nice about being a receptionist that I can't just pick

1141
00:54:07.440 --> 00:54:08.540
one and say that it's my favorite.

1142
00:54:08.660 --> 00:54:10.240
But you probably feel the same way about being a boss.

1143
00:54:10.320 --> 00:54:10.900
You can't pick one.

1144
00:54:11.540 --> 00:54:12.600
Did you have a favorite age?

1145
00:54:13.620 --> 00:54:14.340
Or month?

1146
00:54:15.880 --> 00:54:16.980
An age or month?

1147
00:54:16.980 --> 00:54:18.420
Yeah, like a favorite month.

1148
00:54:18.560 --> 00:54:21.420
Like I, like, April when I was seven.

1149
00:54:21.860 --> 00:54:23.440
I don't have a favorite month now.

1150
00:54:23.720 --> 00:54:25.320
It's sort of like every month is different.

1151
00:54:26.360 --> 00:54:28.540
I could listen to it forever.

1152
00:54:29.020 --> 00:54:30.040
It's so delightful.

1153
00:54:30.380 --> 00:54:31.840
It's such a wonderful free association.

1154
00:54:32.080 --> 00:54:33.760
She holds up the remote control.

1155
00:54:33.960 --> 00:54:35.440
She fishes it out of her bag.

1156
00:54:35.760 --> 00:54:40.060
And the look on Steve's face as Michael when he's like,

1157
00:54:40.200 --> 00:54:41.960
what do you want me to do with it?

1158
00:54:42.060 --> 00:54:44.260
What do I do with all of this?

1159
00:54:44.860 --> 00:54:47.240
We got a fan question from Jenna R.

1160
00:54:47.480 --> 00:54:48.860
in Los Angeles, California.

1161
00:54:48.860 --> 00:54:49.520
Hi, Jenna.

1162
00:54:50.560 --> 00:54:53.280
Where did they film Michael and Aaron's lunch scene?

1163
00:54:53.600 --> 00:54:58.440
It was filmed at a restaurant in Encino called Boca, which has since closed.

1164
00:54:58.680 --> 00:55:01.320
It is now called Monaco Encino.

1165
00:55:01.940 --> 00:55:05.280
And Randy even sent us a photo from their location scout.

1166
00:55:05.520 --> 00:55:09.440
So what they would have done a week prior to an episode where we have to shoot something

1167
00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:12.280
on location, everybody would get in a little van.

1168
00:55:12.280 --> 00:55:16.020
The director, the writer, the producers, the camera operators.

1169
00:55:16.300 --> 00:55:21.460
And they would go around to like three or four restaurants that are options to shoot at

1170
00:55:21.460 --> 00:55:24.580
that our locations manager, Kyle Alexander, would have found.

1171
00:55:24.880 --> 00:55:28.980
And they would sit in them and they would talk about like, we could put the camera here.

1172
00:55:29.140 --> 00:55:31.760
This is what you would see if you put the camera here in this location.

1173
00:55:32.000 --> 00:55:34.420
And then after that, they'd pick the one they like.

1174
00:55:35.100 --> 00:55:38.180
Randy sent us a picture from the location scout.

1175
00:55:38.400 --> 00:55:39.940
You can see Steve in it.

1176
00:55:39.940 --> 00:55:43.740
You can see our first AD, Rusty, talking about how they might shoot the scene in the

1177
00:55:43.740 --> 00:55:44.160
background.

1178
00:55:44.360 --> 00:55:48.300
And then Randy is sitting at a table pretending to be Michael.

1179
00:55:48.620 --> 00:55:53.060
And our second AD, Jenny O'Keefe, is sitting pretending to be Aaron.

1180
00:55:53.320 --> 00:55:54.500
Oh, I love that.

1181
00:55:54.660 --> 00:55:56.080
It just warmed my heart.

1182
00:55:56.220 --> 00:55:57.580
Oh, we'll have to put it in stories.

1183
00:55:57.760 --> 00:55:58.040
Definitely.

1184
00:55:59.140 --> 00:56:04.440
Well, I think we should take a break because when we come back, Michael is going to put

1185
00:56:04.440 --> 00:56:05.180
his foot in his mouth.

1186
00:56:05.360 --> 00:56:06.400
Oh my gosh.

1187
00:56:06.780 --> 00:56:07.980
He sure is.

1188
00:56:07.980 --> 00:56:10.940
And Aaron is going to have quite the reaction.

1189
00:56:20.160 --> 00:56:21.020
We're back.

1190
00:56:21.260 --> 00:56:24.100
Aaron says, tell me about Andy before I met him.

1191
00:56:24.580 --> 00:56:25.140
Oh no.

1192
00:56:25.320 --> 00:56:27.220
She's got like those dreamy eyes.

1193
00:56:27.520 --> 00:56:28.820
Michael's like, let's see.

1194
00:56:28.920 --> 00:56:29.860
Andy plays the banjo.

1195
00:56:30.060 --> 00:56:31.360
She's like, yeah, I love that.

1196
00:56:31.920 --> 00:56:35.360
Other than the fact that he dated Angela, I don't think he's a snappy dresser.

1197
00:56:35.860 --> 00:56:36.840
Aaron's like, what?

1198
00:56:37.540 --> 00:56:41.000
And then Michael has what is my favorite line of the whole episode.

1199
00:56:41.120 --> 00:56:41.400
Same.

1200
00:56:41.400 --> 00:56:44.420
He says, I don't think he's the best dresser.

1201
00:56:44.560 --> 00:56:45.580
Reminds me of Easter.

1202
00:56:45.840 --> 00:56:47.500
I can't unsee this now.

1203
00:56:47.920 --> 00:56:52.860
All of his outfits are like pastel and like beige and pinks and light blues.

1204
00:56:53.100 --> 00:56:54.640
He does dress like Easter.

1205
00:56:54.900 --> 00:56:55.120
He does.

1206
00:56:56.280 --> 00:56:58.660
But Aaron is like, that's not what I meant.

1207
00:56:58.820 --> 00:56:59.040
Yeah.

1208
00:56:59.300 --> 00:57:00.820
I meant the thing about Angela.

1209
00:57:01.100 --> 00:57:04.980
At the same time, the waiter has come by to drop off their food.

1210
00:57:04.980 --> 00:57:06.780
Yeah, he's like, here we go, hot plate.

1211
00:57:06.980 --> 00:57:09.720
And all of this chaos is starting to happen.

1212
00:57:10.720 --> 00:57:12.280
Michael is not picking up on it.

1213
00:57:12.440 --> 00:57:17.680
Instead, he is frustrated that he asked for pickles, but there's only like five or six on this plate.

1214
00:57:18.180 --> 00:57:22.000
To which the waiter says, I will bring you a bowl of pickles.

1215
00:57:22.160 --> 00:57:22.320
Yeah.

1216
00:57:22.960 --> 00:57:26.500
And then Aaron is going to hide inside of her hair.

1217
00:57:26.860 --> 00:57:27.220
Yes.

1218
00:57:27.360 --> 00:57:28.660
And that was in the shooting draft.

1219
00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:32.200
It specifically said that Aaron covers her face with her hair.

1220
00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:32.700
Yes.

1221
00:57:33.220 --> 00:57:34.700
I have a fun catch.

1222
00:57:34.980 --> 00:57:38.900
The waiter in the scene was played by our writer, Aaron Schur.

1223
00:57:39.280 --> 00:57:41.980
You guys know him as the master of the cold opens.

1224
00:57:42.280 --> 00:57:42.480
Yeah.

1225
00:57:42.580 --> 00:57:47.300
He was the go-to guy for cold opens and gave us some of our most famous cold opens.

1226
00:57:47.500 --> 00:57:47.720
Yes.

1227
00:57:47.860 --> 00:57:49.260
The Kevin spilling the chili.

1228
00:57:49.520 --> 00:57:50.200
He wrote that.

1229
00:57:50.420 --> 00:57:52.000
He wrote the speed meter.

1230
00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:55.540
Where everyone's trying to run in front to see how fast they can run.

1231
00:57:56.240 --> 00:58:02.140
So Mindy said that Aaron getting cast as the waiter happened the day before we were set to shoot

1232
00:58:02.140 --> 00:58:03.260
these restaurant scenes.

1233
00:58:03.960 --> 00:58:09.580
She said at first they were going to cast like a young actor, but everybody just looked too Hollywood.

1234
00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:12.120
This was supposed to be a restaurant in Scranton.

1235
00:58:12.700 --> 00:58:18.460
And so then in the writer's room, they pitched, maybe it would be really funny if the waiter in

1236
00:58:18.460 --> 00:58:21.820
the restaurant were like really, really, really, really old.

1237
00:58:23.080 --> 00:58:28.220
She said, quote, like the night at the end of Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade.

1238
00:58:28.600 --> 00:58:29.680
Oh my gosh.

1239
00:58:29.800 --> 00:58:30.360
Super old.

1240
00:58:30.580 --> 00:58:32.220
That's crazy old.

1241
00:58:32.220 --> 00:58:36.200
But Steve Carell thought that might be distracting to the scene.

1242
00:58:36.580 --> 00:58:41.300
So they decided to cast someone who was not too young and not too old.

1243
00:58:41.680 --> 00:58:47.800
And right at that moment of making that decision, Mindy said that our writer, Aaron Schur, got up,

1244
00:58:48.020 --> 00:58:50.200
walked across the room and went to the bathroom.

1245
00:58:50.620 --> 00:58:52.900
And everyone was like, how about Aaron?

1246
00:58:53.300 --> 00:58:54.300
Oh my gosh.

1247
00:58:54.300 --> 00:58:56.260
He is neither too old or too young.

1248
00:59:02.220 --> 00:59:03.600
Walked by the writer's room.

1249
00:59:04.860 --> 00:59:07.420
So Mindy said that he read for it.

1250
00:59:07.620 --> 00:59:08.400
He got the part.

1251
00:59:08.580 --> 00:59:11.300
She also pointed out that he is a trained actor.

1252
00:59:12.240 --> 00:59:18.460
Well, I reached out to Aaron Schur to ask him about this story and he confirms it.

1253
00:59:18.760 --> 00:59:24.460
But he thinks that there might be something else at play, which was that in the weeks before this

1254
00:59:24.460 --> 00:59:26.280
moment, he decided to grow a beard.

1255
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:31.040
He thinks maybe the beard had something to do with it and he's going to explain why.

1256
00:59:32.220 --> 00:59:33.400
Hello, office ladies.

1257
00:59:33.600 --> 00:59:34.480
It's Aaron Schur.

1258
00:59:34.720 --> 00:59:38.700
I'm going to tell you the exciting story about how I became a waiter on The Office.

1259
00:59:39.020 --> 00:59:43.760
I had done a little bit of acting, but mostly I was a stand-up and improviser, a street

1260
00:59:43.760 --> 00:59:45.420
performer, even a circus clown.

1261
00:59:45.580 --> 00:59:51.460
And the audiences all said pretty much the same thing to me, which is you should be a writer.

1262
00:59:51.740 --> 00:59:54.880
So that's what I did because I'm more of a back office sort of guy.

1263
00:59:54.880 --> 01:00:01.080
But as you know, Dunder Mifflin has the annex, which is there just so that people like Mindy,

1264
01:00:01.200 --> 01:00:06.000
Paul, and BJ, who are all writer actors, they had somewhere to be behind a door.

1265
01:00:06.060 --> 01:00:09.660
So there was a reason why we didn't wonder where they were when they were actually in

1266
01:00:09.660 --> 01:00:11.400
the writer's room making the show.

1267
01:00:11.720 --> 01:00:16.500
So when you're on the show, it's easy to start to think maybe there's room in the annex for me too.

1268
01:00:16.720 --> 01:00:18.360
Maybe I could also be a star.

1269
01:00:18.760 --> 01:00:20.220
Obviously, that was not going to happen.

1270
01:00:20.220 --> 01:00:25.300
And so at a certain point, I grew a beard, which is a daring thing to do in Hollywood,

1271
01:00:25.300 --> 01:00:27.580
where you're supposed to always look as young as possible.

1272
01:00:27.940 --> 01:00:31.700
And that's when Mindy came in with her script and was like,

1273
01:00:31.840 --> 01:00:33.860
hey, Aaron, could you read this restaurant scene?

1274
01:00:34.080 --> 01:00:36.580
And I'm like, you want me to criticize your scene?

1275
01:00:36.660 --> 01:00:38.080
And she's like, no, I want you to audition.

1276
01:00:38.420 --> 01:00:40.340
And so she pulled me into the other room.

1277
01:00:40.400 --> 01:00:43.560
And there's Steve Carell, who's going to be directing this episode.

1278
01:00:43.880 --> 01:00:45.940
And I read the scene with him.

1279
01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:46.880
And I'm terrified.

1280
01:00:46.880 --> 01:00:48.440
So I do a terrible job.

1281
01:00:48.440 --> 01:00:50.320
And yet they cast me.

1282
01:00:50.480 --> 01:00:52.680
So the next week, I'm on set.

1283
01:00:53.020 --> 01:00:56.000
And they send me to Hair and Makeup, the Hair and Makeup trailer.

1284
01:00:56.280 --> 01:01:01.400
And when I walk in, they go, oh, it's our old waiter.

1285
01:01:01.920 --> 01:01:05.500
So the beard, it turns out, actually got me the job.

1286
01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:09.100
And then they started to trim the beard and kept trimming it.

1287
01:01:09.220 --> 01:01:10.540
I was in there for like three hours.

1288
01:01:10.820 --> 01:01:11.880
And I got a little paranoid.

1289
01:01:12.040 --> 01:01:15.720
Like, is this all because my beard was annoying Steve?

1290
01:01:15.720 --> 01:01:20.860
And he just cast me in an evil plot to get my beard to not look so scraggly?

1291
01:01:21.120 --> 01:01:22.300
Of course, that wasn't it.

1292
01:01:23.340 --> 01:01:28.100
Okay, but I want to say, Erin, I hear you.

1293
01:01:28.220 --> 01:01:31.780
Because remember when Ryan went blonde?

1294
01:01:32.260 --> 01:01:32.660
Yeah.

1295
01:01:33.160 --> 01:01:37.160
That was because Mindy thought it would be funny for BJ to have to dye his hair blonde.

1296
01:01:37.760 --> 01:01:41.600
So they created this whole plot for why the character would do it.

1297
01:01:41.720 --> 01:01:44.940
So maybe Mindy was like, that beard needs a trim and a tidy.

1298
01:01:45.460 --> 01:01:45.800
Exactly.

1299
01:01:45.940 --> 01:01:47.320
How can I do that?

1300
01:01:47.440 --> 01:01:47.940
You know what?

1301
01:01:47.940 --> 01:01:49.460
I'm going to write him into an episode.

1302
01:01:50.520 --> 01:01:53.660
I also asked Erin what it was like to shoot the scene.

1303
01:01:53.860 --> 01:01:56.620
I wanted to know, like, did you get much direction?

1304
01:01:57.080 --> 01:02:00.260
And he said they pretty much let him do his own thing.

1305
01:02:00.620 --> 01:02:02.800
But that actually led to some probleMs.

1306
01:02:03.020 --> 01:02:04.260
But I'll let him explain.

1307
01:02:04.960 --> 01:02:09.340
Once I get on the actual set, I'm determined to do a good job for obvious reasons.

1308
01:02:09.340 --> 01:02:13.260
But also because there's a lot of hardworking actors out there who could have used this opportunity.

1309
01:02:13.260 --> 01:02:15.700
And I owe it to them to at least do a decent job.

1310
01:02:15.840 --> 01:02:25.900
And also as a writer, I know how easy it is for an actor who has only a few lines to ruin a scene because they're nervous or because they think it's their star vehicle.

1311
01:02:26.020 --> 01:02:27.560
So I'm going to do a good job.

1312
01:02:27.680 --> 01:02:29.080
And Steve is directing it.

1313
01:02:29.160 --> 01:02:31.840
But he assumes I know enough to do my own blocking.

1314
01:02:32.080 --> 01:02:35.200
So I come up with my own, which is blocking is how you move around the set, right?

1315
01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:40.940
And I come up with my own blocking and I did the dumbest thing, which is I started way back in the kitchen.

1316
01:02:41.140 --> 01:02:42.540
I'm not even in the room.

1317
01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:45.040
So all I can hear back there is Steve Yell action.

1318
01:02:45.180 --> 01:02:48.680
And then I've got to walk in and I can't hear what's being said at the table.

1319
01:02:48.800 --> 01:02:51.220
And I got to find a way to land right on my cue.

1320
01:02:51.880 --> 01:02:53.460
But this is my plan.

1321
01:02:53.660 --> 01:02:55.240
I realized, OK, here's what I'm going to do.

1322
01:02:55.440 --> 01:02:59.320
So my plan was I'm going to hide behind B camera.

1323
01:02:59.580 --> 01:03:02.120
There's usually we had two cameras shooting simultaneously.

1324
01:03:02.700 --> 01:03:07.620
And so if I'm behind B camera, I won't be in the shot because camera A isn't going to film camera B.

1325
01:03:07.780 --> 01:03:08.860
That's not how the pros do it.

1326
01:03:09.220 --> 01:03:11.980
But I, of course, couldn't be in front of camera B, but you've got to be behind.

1327
01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:17.140
Anyway, when I come out, camera B has been moved to the further side of the restaurant.

1328
01:03:17.380 --> 01:03:21.380
So now there's no way for me not to be on camera and to hear the scene.

1329
01:03:21.540 --> 01:03:27.540
So I come up with this, what I hope seems like a human behavior of circling the table slowly,

1330
01:03:28.080 --> 01:03:29.320
trying to hear what's being said.

1331
01:03:29.320 --> 01:03:34.340
And in this scene, you can see Steve looks over his shoulder, like trying to find this weird lurking waiter.

1332
01:03:34.880 --> 01:03:42.160
And this is proof that I was never an actual waiter because a real waiter knows how to show up at the table at the most awkward moment

1333
01:03:42.160 --> 01:03:44.980
when somebody's heard terrible news and is about to start crying.

1334
01:03:45.160 --> 01:03:47.920
But at the end of it all, I think it went fine.

1335
01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:50.640
And Steve was very kind and told me I did a good job.

1336
01:03:50.780 --> 01:03:52.260
And that meant so much to me.

1337
01:03:52.260 --> 01:03:59.840
I mean, what an opportunity to perform a script written by Mindy, directed by Steve, and to be on The Greatest Show Ever.

1338
01:04:00.020 --> 01:04:02.000
And now I'm on The Greatest Podcast Ever.

1339
01:04:02.160 --> 01:04:03.100
So thank you.

1340
01:04:04.960 --> 01:04:06.100
Thank you, Aaron.

1341
01:04:06.340 --> 01:04:07.560
Aaron, that is so fun.

1342
01:04:07.560 --> 01:04:08.740
And we just love you.

1343
01:04:09.600 --> 01:04:14.860
Also, Aaron said, for the record, he actually likes pickles, but not by the bowl.

1344
01:04:15.380 --> 01:04:26.400
One of his lines that cracked me up, because like he was saying, when you have only a few lines, it's really hard not to make them like the most important things you ever say.

1345
01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:26.820
Yes.

1346
01:04:26.820 --> 01:04:30.400
And he had this line when Michael says, could I get more pickles?

1347
01:04:30.600 --> 01:04:33.100
And his first response is, of course.

1348
01:04:33.720 --> 01:04:36.780
And that, of course, to me, was so perfect.

1349
01:04:37.060 --> 01:04:42.340
Like anyone who's worked in food service knows that moment where you're like, absolutely, sure.

1350
01:04:42.560 --> 01:04:44.160
I would love to do that.

1351
01:04:44.260 --> 01:04:46.020
I would love to get you a bowl of pickles.

1352
01:04:47.100 --> 01:04:49.580
Well, Aaron is really starting to spiral.

1353
01:04:49.860 --> 01:04:53.240
You know, she's got her face covered with her hair.

1354
01:04:53.240 --> 01:04:58.120
Or she's making really heavy groaning sounds like that.

1355
01:04:58.800 --> 01:05:00.520
Michael delivers a famous line.

1356
01:05:00.680 --> 01:05:01.960
It's from When Harry Met Sally.

1357
01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:02.920
Yes.

1358
01:05:03.060 --> 01:05:06.040
He looks around the restaurant and says, I'll have what she's having.

1359
01:05:06.280 --> 01:05:06.680
Mm-hmm.

1360
01:05:06.900 --> 01:05:08.940
I went back and watched the scene after that.

1361
01:05:09.400 --> 01:05:10.400
It's so brilliant.

1362
01:05:10.560 --> 01:05:12.300
It makes me want to rewatch When Harry Met Sally.

1363
01:05:12.520 --> 01:05:14.200
Oh, I rewatched it recently.

1364
01:05:14.260 --> 01:05:15.600
It's a flawless movie.

1365
01:05:15.720 --> 01:05:16.400
It's terrific.

1366
01:05:16.740 --> 01:05:18.260
Office Ladies breaks down movies?

1367
01:05:18.680 --> 01:05:19.120
Yeah.

1368
01:05:19.280 --> 01:05:20.980
We have to do a series of rom-coMs.

1369
01:05:21.040 --> 01:05:23.100
Well, I also just rewatched Dirty Dancing.

1370
01:05:23.600 --> 01:05:24.080
Yeah.

1371
01:05:24.320 --> 01:05:25.740
I want to break down Dirty Dancing.

1372
01:05:26.260 --> 01:05:28.200
Nobody puts baby in a corner.

1373
01:05:28.480 --> 01:05:29.000
Come on.

1374
01:05:29.820 --> 01:05:30.940
It's really incredible.

1375
01:05:31.220 --> 01:05:31.780
We need to watch it.

1376
01:05:32.080 --> 01:05:35.220
Well, it's a very awkward car ride back to the office.

1377
01:05:35.680 --> 01:05:36.760
Oh, is it?

1378
01:05:37.040 --> 01:05:39.160
And, lady, there was more in deleted scenes.

1379
01:05:39.500 --> 01:05:44.440
In the shooting draft, Michael is trying to console Aaron in the car, right?

1380
01:05:44.580 --> 01:05:45.840
He knows he's messed up.

1381
01:05:45.960 --> 01:05:46.240
Mm-hmm.

1382
01:05:46.300 --> 01:05:49.860
He says, you know, I think it's probably best to not say anything about this.

1383
01:05:50.060 --> 01:05:52.060
And Aaron is just, like, stewing.

1384
01:05:52.540 --> 01:05:55.420
He goes on to say, you know, take a beat.

1385
01:05:55.740 --> 01:05:56.440
Calm down.

1386
01:05:56.800 --> 01:05:58.540
Talk to him privately about it.

1387
01:05:58.660 --> 01:05:59.800
Next week or a month.

1388
01:05:59.920 --> 01:06:00.460
Maybe never.

1389
01:06:00.700 --> 01:06:03.500
It would probably make things awkward at work if you bring it up.

1390
01:06:03.760 --> 01:06:05.400
Heck, you might even forget about it.

1391
01:06:05.400 --> 01:06:12.060
And then, I don't know if you've noticed, Jenna, in the car scenes, there's a little patch

1392
01:06:12.060 --> 01:06:14.140
on Michael's seatbelt that's frayed.

1393
01:06:14.300 --> 01:06:15.580
It's right at his shoulder.

1394
01:06:15.860 --> 01:06:16.240
Mm-mm.

1395
01:06:16.240 --> 01:06:20.760
And when I watched it, I did notice this sort of, like, fuzzy thing in a seatbelt.

1396
01:06:20.840 --> 01:06:23.680
And I thought, why would they let that be in the shot?

1397
01:06:23.800 --> 01:06:27.020
Why wouldn't they get him a seatbelt that wasn't damaged?

1398
01:06:27.820 --> 01:06:32.960
Well, in deleted scenes, Michael says, sometimes I chew on my seatbelt when I'm upset.

1399
01:06:33.200 --> 01:06:34.580
You can feel free to do that.

1400
01:06:35.020 --> 01:06:36.100
Aaron does not respond.

1401
01:06:36.380 --> 01:06:39.440
And then Michael shows her and starts to chew on his seatbelt.

1402
01:06:40.020 --> 01:06:44.060
So they actually had to put chew marks on the seatbelt on purpose.

1403
01:06:44.320 --> 01:06:44.700
Yes.

1404
01:06:45.040 --> 01:06:45.500
Wow.

1405
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:47.140
And it's in deleted scenes.

1406
01:06:47.340 --> 01:06:49.580
Michael, like, puts his seatbelt in his mouth.

1407
01:06:49.940 --> 01:06:53.100
Anyway, that seatbelt was damaged on purpose.

1408
01:06:53.540 --> 01:06:56.720
Well, when they get back to the office, Pam's milk is coming in.

1409
01:06:56.840 --> 01:06:57.540
She's uncomfortable.

1410
01:06:57.560 --> 01:06:59.040
She wants to pump.

1411
01:06:59.240 --> 01:07:00.640
But her pump is missing.

1412
01:07:01.060 --> 01:07:01.540
Yeah.

1413
01:07:01.780 --> 01:07:02.740
Guess who has it?

1414
01:07:03.260 --> 01:07:04.660
This was so crazy.

1415
01:07:04.680 --> 01:07:06.820
I forgot about the scene.

1416
01:07:06.820 --> 01:07:10.960
I forgot that Meredith took Pam's breast pump.

1417
01:07:11.180 --> 01:07:12.300
Because it feels good.

1418
01:07:12.800 --> 01:07:14.200
She likes how it feels.

1419
01:07:14.900 --> 01:07:15.620
Oh, my gosh.

1420
01:07:15.700 --> 01:07:17.260
Once again, Kate is fearless.

1421
01:07:17.820 --> 01:07:18.000
Yeah.

1422
01:07:18.680 --> 01:07:20.720
So Pam is like, it's not sterile.

1423
01:07:20.840 --> 01:07:21.700
She's very upset.

1424
01:07:22.400 --> 01:07:26.340
And then Dwight is going to offer to hand express the milk.

1425
01:07:27.140 --> 01:07:28.500
He's going to get it out for her.

1426
01:07:28.660 --> 01:07:28.840
Yeah.

1427
01:07:29.500 --> 01:07:30.580
She's like, no, thank you.

1428
01:07:30.760 --> 01:07:31.080
No, thank you.

1429
01:07:31.480 --> 01:07:36.720
Jenna, when I watched the scene, all I could think about was the time when I was back on set

1430
01:07:36.720 --> 01:07:41.520
after having Isabel and I was breastfeeding and we were taking breaks so I could breastfeed.

1431
01:07:41.740 --> 01:07:43.700
Kelly Cantley helped make that happen.

1432
01:07:44.180 --> 01:07:45.680
And we were in the conference room.

1433
01:07:45.820 --> 01:07:46.880
We were in there all day.

1434
01:07:47.100 --> 01:07:49.540
And someone said, hey, what time is it?

1435
01:07:49.780 --> 01:07:53.460
And I touched the side of my boobs and I said, about 11 a.m.

1436
01:07:54.380 --> 01:07:56.640
And then they were like, yeah, it's 1059.

1437
01:07:57.000 --> 01:07:57.740
Do you remember that?

1438
01:07:57.840 --> 01:07:58.180
Yes.

1439
01:07:58.660 --> 01:08:03.020
We all started cracking up and like doing this bit that I could tell time by.

1440
01:08:03.380 --> 01:08:03.600
Yeah.

1441
01:08:03.700 --> 01:08:05.420
We would be like, Angela, what time is it?

1442
01:08:06.560 --> 01:08:09.720
We started testing you and you were very accurate.

1443
01:08:10.060 --> 01:08:11.720
Because I had my whole pump schedule.

1444
01:08:11.920 --> 01:08:12.120
Yeah.

1445
01:08:12.240 --> 01:08:14.800
And your milk really does come in on a schedule.

1446
01:08:15.060 --> 01:08:15.160
Yeah.

1447
01:08:15.940 --> 01:08:24.220
Well, incidentally, you know, my mom told me that when I was born back in 1974, not as many women nursed their babies back then.

1448
01:08:24.360 --> 01:08:28.580
But it was something that she was open to and she had done some research on.

1449
01:08:28.820 --> 01:08:34.580
And she said when I was about two months old, her and my dad wanted to go out to dinner for the first time.

1450
01:08:34.740 --> 01:08:36.820
She said they hired their very first babysitter.

1451
01:08:36.820 --> 01:08:47.240
And in order to leave for that period of time for dinner, it took her an entire week of self-expressing, using her hand, one bottle of milk.

1452
01:08:47.380 --> 01:08:52.440
She kept it in the freezer so that the babysitter could defrost it and give it to me.

1453
01:08:52.780 --> 01:08:53.900
Oh, my gosh.

1454
01:08:54.140 --> 01:08:54.440
Yeah.

1455
01:08:54.880 --> 01:08:56.760
The things our moms did for us.

1456
01:08:56.860 --> 01:08:57.220
I know.

1457
01:08:58.160 --> 01:09:06.300
Oh, incidentally, I will say, Mindy also said that the idea that Meredith would steal Pam's breast pump was a pitch from Charlie Grandy.

1458
01:09:09.050 --> 01:09:11.510
Andy is going to ask Aaron how lunch went.

1459
01:09:11.710 --> 01:09:13.790
And she is very cold to him.

1460
01:09:14.230 --> 01:09:17.170
She then completely bites Oscar's head off.

1461
01:09:17.290 --> 01:09:19.430
Oscar says, I think we're out of fax cover sheets.

1462
01:09:19.590 --> 01:09:22.050
And she says, God, Oscar, will you keep your pants on?

1463
01:09:22.230 --> 01:09:22.990
It's easy.

1464
01:09:23.570 --> 01:09:27.930
At 9 minutes, 48 seconds, you guys, Oscar looks right to camera.

1465
01:09:27.930 --> 01:09:28.990
Like, what the hell?

1466
01:09:29.470 --> 01:09:31.710
But Oscar never looked right to camera.

1467
01:09:31.850 --> 01:09:34.090
So this was really fun to spot.

1468
01:09:34.110 --> 01:09:36.170
And I just loved him in that moment.

1469
01:09:36.410 --> 01:09:37.030
I love that.

1470
01:09:37.030 --> 01:09:43.350
Well, now we're going to go to the conference room because there is a Secretary's Day party underway in Aaron's honor.

1471
01:09:43.590 --> 01:09:46.130
Her face is on a cake.

1472
01:09:46.310 --> 01:09:46.710
Yeah.

1473
01:09:47.010 --> 01:09:49.710
And I think also it's on the plates.

1474
01:09:50.270 --> 01:09:51.290
Oh, no way.

1475
01:09:51.290 --> 01:09:56.330
I mean, it's a very elaborate party, all thrown by Angela.

1476
01:09:56.850 --> 01:09:57.610
Yes.

1477
01:09:58.090 --> 01:09:58.670
Wait.

1478
01:09:59.030 --> 01:10:02.090
Is she the head of the PPC again?

1479
01:10:02.250 --> 01:10:03.550
That's what I'm wondering.

1480
01:10:04.070 --> 01:10:05.550
Oh, wow.

1481
01:10:05.550 --> 01:10:07.930
They slid that right in there.

1482
01:10:08.430 --> 01:10:13.170
There was a couplet of dialogue between Ryan and Kelly in the scene.

1483
01:10:13.170 --> 01:10:16.590
And as I watched it, I was like, that's just BJ and Mindy.

1484
01:10:17.050 --> 01:10:18.130
Which one was it?

1485
01:10:18.290 --> 01:10:20.830
They're talking about the Cookie Monster parody.

1486
01:10:21.690 --> 01:10:23.850
And Kelly does her version of it.

1487
01:10:24.330 --> 01:10:26.570
And Ryan goes, that's a little derivative.

1488
01:10:26.950 --> 01:10:30.010
And Kelly says, but parody is always derivative.

1489
01:10:30.290 --> 01:10:32.190
And Ryan says, it's not organic.

1490
01:10:32.450 --> 01:10:33.130
Do you know what I mean?

1491
01:10:33.130 --> 01:10:36.170
And that just sounded like a conversation between the two of them.

1492
01:10:36.290 --> 01:10:39.470
That could have been a conversation that we would hear them having on set.

1493
01:10:39.570 --> 01:10:39.910
Yes.

1494
01:10:40.410 --> 01:10:40.870
100%.

1495
01:10:41.390 --> 01:10:45.410
So, you know, in this scene, Andy is going to put on his guitar.

1496
01:10:45.830 --> 01:10:47.770
He's going to put on his harmonica.

1497
01:10:47.950 --> 01:10:51.410
And he's going to sing Aaron a song called Secretary of Love.

1498
01:10:51.650 --> 01:10:54.330
I had a question about the harmonica bit of it all.

1499
01:10:54.550 --> 01:10:54.830
Uh-huh.

1500
01:10:55.050 --> 01:10:57.270
He never straps on a harmonica.

1501
01:10:57.850 --> 01:11:02.950
I think it was a little scheme to make sure the cake stayed up around his face.

1502
01:11:03.130 --> 01:11:04.590
Well, it was in the script.

1503
01:11:04.830 --> 01:11:06.030
I looked it up.

1504
01:11:06.350 --> 01:11:10.990
It says, Andy gets his guitar and one of those harmonicas attached to headgear.

1505
01:11:11.370 --> 01:11:15.550
And Andy begins to sing an original song called Secretary of Love.

1506
01:11:15.750 --> 01:11:18.630
It has a feel of Ricky Nelson's Travelin' Man.

1507
01:11:19.210 --> 01:11:24.890
In the interview on Office Tally, Mindy mentioned that she wrote lyrics for the song Secretary of Love.

1508
01:11:25.110 --> 01:11:27.230
And they were in the table redraft.

1509
01:11:27.570 --> 01:11:30.030
And Ed does play the harmonica.

1510
01:11:30.030 --> 01:11:32.410
And they had intended for him to play it.

1511
01:11:32.690 --> 01:11:33.030
Okay.

1512
01:11:33.130 --> 01:11:34.490
Here are the lyrics.

1513
01:11:34.750 --> 01:11:35.550
Oh, my gosh.

1514
01:11:36.350 --> 01:11:43.950
There's the Secretary of Labor, Secretary of Health, Health and Human Resources just asked me on a date.

1515
01:11:44.510 --> 01:11:47.330
Secretary of Energy keeps on a-winking at me.

1516
01:11:47.490 --> 01:11:51.010
But I can't keep my hands off of homeland security.

1517
01:11:51.710 --> 01:11:55.210
But all the different secretaries that I've taken to my bed.

1518
01:11:55.490 --> 01:11:59.130
There's only one secretary I can't get out of my head.

1519
01:11:59.130 --> 01:12:02.730
The red-haired secretary is the one I sing of.

1520
01:12:02.950 --> 01:12:07.790
She's my Dunder Mifflin secretary, my secretary of love.

1521
01:12:08.270 --> 01:12:09.650
Oh, my gosh.

1522
01:12:10.090 --> 01:12:17.330
I mean, in some ways it's good that he didn't sing it because Aaron already thinks he slept with everyone in the office.

1523
01:12:17.610 --> 01:12:18.730
She's like, Phyllis, Kelly?

1524
01:12:50.160 --> 01:12:51.560
Pam?

1525
01:12:51.560 --> 01:12:52.700
During our interview with Ellie.

1526
01:12:53.140 --> 01:12:57.140
But I also found a little tidbit from Mindy on Office Tally about it.

1527
01:12:57.580 --> 01:13:00.520
She said that the cake was really dense.

1528
01:13:00.800 --> 01:13:01.140
Yeah.

1529
01:13:01.140 --> 01:13:05.820
And that the first time Ellie threw it at Ed, it made a really loud sound.

1530
01:13:06.040 --> 01:13:07.640
It sounded like, whack.

1531
01:13:07.920 --> 01:13:09.760
That's why we reacted like that.

1532
01:13:11.420 --> 01:13:14.140
We had a fan question from Mary Kay in Portland, Oregon.

1533
01:13:15.360 --> 01:13:19.560
I think the real question we all want to know the answer to is, how good was that cake?

1534
01:13:19.560 --> 01:13:20.800
Because it looks delicious.

1535
01:13:21.200 --> 01:13:22.420
I really ate that cake.

1536
01:13:22.580 --> 01:13:22.880
Me too.

1537
01:13:22.960 --> 01:13:23.540
It was delicious.

1538
01:13:23.740 --> 01:13:24.360
It was so good.

1539
01:13:24.500 --> 01:13:25.320
Mary, good call.

1540
01:13:25.440 --> 01:13:25.940
It was great.

1541
01:13:26.540 --> 01:13:29.220
Well, people are going to start trying to make Aaron feel better.

1542
01:13:29.220 --> 01:13:32.420
Kevin tries to console her slash hit on her.

1543
01:13:32.780 --> 01:13:37.040
And while that is happening, Gabe overhears Pam doing an impression of Kevin.

1544
01:13:37.320 --> 01:13:41.400
I want to point out when Jim laughs, that was John's laugh.

1545
01:13:41.700 --> 01:13:42.020
Yeah.

1546
01:13:42.640 --> 01:13:44.680
That is exactly how he starts to laugh.

1547
01:13:44.840 --> 01:13:45.140
It's true.

1548
01:13:46.180 --> 01:13:47.320
Gabe is going to suspend them.

1549
01:13:47.920 --> 01:13:48.180
Mm-hmm.

1550
01:13:48.660 --> 01:13:50.040
He suspends Pam.

1551
01:13:50.260 --> 01:13:51.240
He suspends Jim.

1552
01:13:51.440 --> 01:13:55.340
And then he even is going to suspend Dwight for slow clapping the suspension.

1553
01:13:55.760 --> 01:13:56.920
Kevin is so happy.

1554
01:13:57.020 --> 01:13:58.400
He says C is for suspension.

1555
01:13:59.220 --> 01:13:59.560
Oh, Kevin.

1556
01:14:01.020 --> 01:14:06.280
Meanwhile, in Michael's office, Andy has a great line where he's like, I don't understand

1557
01:14:06.280 --> 01:14:11.360
how my past engagement came up in your restaurant talk.

1558
01:14:11.660 --> 01:14:12.140
Yeah.

1559
01:14:12.280 --> 01:14:13.260
It's Secretary's Day.

1560
01:14:13.440 --> 01:14:14.520
How did this come up?

1561
01:14:14.800 --> 01:14:16.300
But I'm with Michael.

1562
01:14:16.740 --> 01:14:19.460
Like, why did you keep this a secret from her?

1563
01:14:19.620 --> 01:14:22.000
How is Michael supposed to know that she doesn't know?

1564
01:14:22.120 --> 01:14:25.520
This is not, I think, an example of Michael revealing a secret.

1565
01:14:25.940 --> 01:14:26.200
Right.

1566
01:14:26.420 --> 01:14:28.080
Like he has been known to do in the paSt.

1567
01:14:28.200 --> 01:14:28.380
Right.

1568
01:14:28.860 --> 01:14:29.220
Exactly.

1569
01:14:29.440 --> 01:14:31.940
Michael didn't even know this was an off-topic subject.

1570
01:14:32.480 --> 01:14:32.680
Yeah.

1571
01:14:33.140 --> 01:14:36.100
Well, Andy is now going to have a very agonizing talking head.

1572
01:14:36.280 --> 01:14:37.260
He's like, who cares?

1573
01:14:37.340 --> 01:14:38.060
It'll blow over.

1574
01:14:38.300 --> 01:14:39.100
Maybe I should have told her.

1575
01:14:39.260 --> 01:14:40.180
Everybody does stupid things.

1576
01:14:40.240 --> 01:14:41.340
He's like all over the map.

1577
01:14:41.340 --> 01:14:46.900
Well, it's actually like a series of talking heads sort of intercut into one talking head,

1578
01:14:47.000 --> 01:14:48.640
which I'm not sure we've ever seen before.

1579
01:14:48.880 --> 01:14:49.140
Yeah.

1580
01:14:49.260 --> 01:14:56.720
I just wanted to point out that at the top of the episode, at 1 minute 20 seconds, Andy

1581
01:14:56.720 --> 01:15:04.060
says that it's not only Secretary's Day, but it's also he and Aaron's three-week anniversary.

1582
01:15:04.060 --> 01:15:07.060
And I just want to put this out there.

1583
01:15:07.560 --> 01:15:14.200
I think maybe if you've just been dating someone for three weeks and they go to such

1584
01:15:14.200 --> 01:15:22.980
effort to celebrate you on Secretary's Day, maybe you can say, hey, why didn't you tell

1585
01:15:22.980 --> 01:15:27.020
me about this previous relationship that really upset me?

1586
01:15:27.660 --> 01:15:29.380
It's only been three weeks, you guys.

1587
01:15:29.540 --> 01:15:31.240
I think there's still some discovery.

1588
01:15:31.520 --> 01:15:32.280
Am I wrong?

1589
01:15:32.560 --> 01:15:38.120
Well, it's interesting you asked this question because we got mail from both Liza A.

1590
01:15:38.220 --> 01:15:38.480
in North

1591
01:15:38.480 --> 01:15:39.740
Carolina and Paul W.

1592
01:15:39.800 --> 01:15:45.560
in Chicago asking, if you were Andy, would you have told Aaron that

1593
01:15:45.560 --> 01:15:48.000
you were once engaged or would you have waited?

1594
01:15:48.400 --> 01:15:52.060
And do you agree with Aaron's decision to break up with him because of this?

1595
01:15:52.380 --> 01:15:56.280
Well, listen, I think it would have been a big flipping conversation.

1596
01:15:56.280 --> 01:15:57.920
I would have been upset.

1597
01:15:58.300 --> 01:16:03.100
But at three weeks, I might have understood that maybe he was waiting for the right moment

1598
01:16:03.100 --> 01:16:04.040
to tell me.

1599
01:16:04.720 --> 01:16:08.960
I have to say, I 100% understand Aaron's reaction.

1600
01:16:09.560 --> 01:16:15.340
It's not just that he didn't tell her that he's been engaged before, but this is a co-worker

1601
01:16:15.340 --> 01:16:17.500
that she sees every day.

1602
01:16:17.760 --> 01:16:19.880
So I think that that makes it different.

1603
01:16:20.100 --> 01:16:24.100
I think that's something that you need to say right away.

1604
01:16:24.660 --> 01:16:25.860
You know, I agree.

1605
01:16:26.160 --> 01:16:31.220
Like, if you've just started dating someone maybe around, I don't know, around this time,

1606
01:16:31.380 --> 01:16:34.640
three weeks, a month, you might say, oh, you know, I was engaged before.

1607
01:16:34.840 --> 01:16:35.000
Yeah.

1608
01:16:35.260 --> 01:16:38.360
Here's all my business because we've lasted three weeks.

1609
01:16:38.520 --> 01:16:40.220
Maybe we're going to make a real go of it.

1610
01:16:40.560 --> 01:16:41.440
Here's everything.

1611
01:16:42.200 --> 01:16:42.500
Right.

1612
01:16:42.500 --> 01:16:46.420
But not if the situation is like, oh, hey, you should know.

1613
01:16:46.420 --> 01:16:49.040
Oh, I actually used to be engaged to my roommate.

1614
01:16:49.720 --> 01:16:50.120
Yeah.

1615
01:16:50.320 --> 01:16:51.360
You know, like, that's like that.

1616
01:16:51.480 --> 01:16:54.360
Like, oh, I used to be engaged to this person right next to you.

1617
01:16:54.460 --> 01:16:54.640
Right.

1618
01:16:54.740 --> 01:16:56.400
And everyone in this room knows.

1619
01:16:56.480 --> 01:16:56.680
Yes.

1620
01:16:56.740 --> 01:16:57.140
But you.

1621
01:16:57.320 --> 01:16:58.100
That's the difference.

1622
01:16:58.260 --> 01:16:58.420
Yeah.

1623
01:16:58.520 --> 01:16:59.260
I see that.

1624
01:16:59.400 --> 01:17:00.860
But do you think it's breakup worthy?

1625
01:17:01.160 --> 01:17:01.460
Yes.

1626
01:17:01.900 --> 01:17:02.260
Okay.

1627
01:17:02.520 --> 01:17:05.420
I would feel very embarrassed.

1628
01:17:05.860 --> 01:17:06.260
Embarrassed.

1629
01:17:06.440 --> 01:17:09.480
And humiliated and distrustful.

1630
01:17:09.680 --> 01:17:10.000
Yeah.

1631
01:17:10.560 --> 01:17:11.140
Of like.

1632
01:17:11.260 --> 01:17:11.480
Right.

1633
01:17:16.420 --> 01:17:16.680
Yeah.

1634
01:17:16.820 --> 01:17:18.540
It's because they're in the same office.

1635
01:17:19.440 --> 01:17:19.780
Mm-hmm.

1636
01:17:20.620 --> 01:17:24.480
Well, now Angela's going to try to console Aaron as best as she can.

1637
01:17:24.940 --> 01:17:26.360
She's like, psst, hey, Aaron.

1638
01:17:26.560 --> 01:17:27.420
And I love this line.

1639
01:17:27.520 --> 01:17:29.000
Aaron's like, you want to talk to me?

1640
01:17:29.200 --> 01:17:30.100
Come to my desk.

1641
01:17:30.920 --> 01:17:31.320
Yeah.

1642
01:17:31.680 --> 01:17:33.040
She's ready to throw down.

1643
01:17:33.780 --> 01:17:35.420
They have this hilarious dialogue.

1644
01:17:35.420 --> 01:17:40.320
We talked about it with Ellie, where they go back and forth about wanting to throw up just

1645
01:17:40.320 --> 01:17:41.260
thinking about it.

1646
01:17:41.720 --> 01:17:42.120
Yeah.

1647
01:17:42.120 --> 01:17:47.540
And then at the end of the scene, the camera pulls back and Toby is standing there.

1648
01:17:47.740 --> 01:17:49.660
He can't seem to work the fax machine.

1649
01:17:50.040 --> 01:17:53.660
Suddenly, everybody has to fax things today and it's not working well.

1650
01:17:53.900 --> 01:17:54.020
Yeah.

1651
01:17:54.140 --> 01:17:55.620
Everyone's real busy at reception.

1652
01:17:56.500 --> 01:18:02.400
Mindy said that that reveal of Toby having been there for this whole exchange was Steve's

1653
01:18:02.400 --> 01:18:02.740
idea.

1654
01:18:03.100 --> 01:18:04.460
It was really funny.

1655
01:18:05.200 --> 01:18:07.780
Well, now Pam is going to try to console Aaron.

1656
01:18:07.980 --> 01:18:11.180
And I thought she was so like eloquent in this moment.

1657
01:18:11.180 --> 01:18:11.980
I know.

1658
01:18:12.160 --> 01:18:13.660
We talked about this with Ellie, too.

1659
01:18:14.120 --> 01:18:15.740
It doesn't work again.

1660
01:18:16.220 --> 01:18:17.140
It's too bad.

1661
01:18:17.280 --> 01:18:20.700
But then Pam is going to walk over and give Jim a kiss.

1662
01:18:20.880 --> 01:18:25.080
And we haven't kind of seen any like kissy kiss between Jim and Pam in a while.

1663
01:18:25.300 --> 01:18:28.560
So I thought this was a really nice kind of romantic moment.

1664
01:18:28.840 --> 01:18:29.760
Kind of took us back.

1665
01:18:29.980 --> 01:18:30.200
Yeah.

1666
01:18:31.060 --> 01:18:32.860
Gabe is going to get some news now.

1667
01:18:33.180 --> 01:18:37.140
At 15 minutes and 48 seconds, he is standing in a hallway.

1668
01:18:37.360 --> 01:18:38.500
He's talking to corporate.

1669
01:18:38.500 --> 01:18:44.820
Randy told me that this was filmed in the stairway directly opposite the door to his office

1670
01:18:44.820 --> 01:18:46.440
in the writer's area.

1671
01:18:46.920 --> 01:18:50.860
He said that Steve Carell chose the stairwell because it was rarely used.

1672
01:18:51.020 --> 01:18:56.240
And Steve thought that it would be good to see Gabe in a setting that was more unfamiliar

1673
01:18:56.240 --> 01:18:56.940
to viewers.

1674
01:18:57.280 --> 01:19:00.840
I love how so much thought goes into every moment.

1675
01:19:01.060 --> 01:19:01.360
Little moment.

1676
01:19:01.620 --> 01:19:01.780
Yeah.

1677
01:19:02.040 --> 01:19:02.360
Yeah.

1678
01:19:02.360 --> 01:19:04.660
When I think of the stairwell, I always think of Dwight.

1679
01:19:05.040 --> 01:19:06.240
Pumping himself up.

1680
01:19:06.240 --> 01:19:06.360
Yeah.

1681
01:19:06.540 --> 01:19:06.920
Exactly.

1682
01:19:07.620 --> 01:19:08.940
Or moaning and wailing.

1683
01:19:09.140 --> 01:19:09.540
Yes.

1684
01:19:09.900 --> 01:19:15.180
Well, on this phone call, Gabe is going to learn that he actually cannot reprimand or suspend

1685
01:19:15.180 --> 01:19:15.800
anyone.

1686
01:19:16.120 --> 01:19:20.800
And then Toby is going to call Pam and tell her the same thing.

1687
01:19:21.740 --> 01:19:26.720
He also says to her, I found out some of the other things they're doing at their, and she

1688
01:19:26.720 --> 01:19:27.380
hangs up on it.

1689
01:19:27.400 --> 01:19:27.580
Yeah.

1690
01:19:28.500 --> 01:19:29.040
I know.

1691
01:19:29.120 --> 01:19:30.680
She's like, I got all the information I need.

1692
01:19:30.820 --> 01:19:35.000
She passes a note to Jim, and now they know exactly what they're going to do.

1693
01:19:35.320 --> 01:19:35.540
Yeah.

1694
01:19:35.780 --> 01:19:37.140
They're going to take their suspension.

1695
01:19:37.460 --> 01:19:37.660
Yeah.

1696
01:19:38.120 --> 01:19:38.520
Paid.

1697
01:19:38.660 --> 01:19:40.800
They're going to go home and think about their behavior.

1698
01:19:41.280 --> 01:19:41.440
Yeah.

1699
01:19:42.460 --> 01:19:47.780
Well, Dwight is going to apologize, but Gabe is running after Pam and Jim.

1700
01:19:47.780 --> 01:19:51.080
He does not want them to leave because now he's got egg on his face.

1701
01:19:51.080 --> 01:19:55.540
When he comes back in the bullpen, Oscar's like, is it me or did they just get a paid

1702
01:19:55.540 --> 01:19:56.220
day off?

1703
01:19:56.440 --> 01:19:56.880
Mm-hmm.

1704
01:19:57.760 --> 01:20:00.820
To which Gabe now tries to do his cookie monster impression.

1705
01:20:01.660 --> 01:20:02.140
Right.

1706
01:20:02.420 --> 01:20:05.260
This leads us to what I'm calling Jedi Kevin.

1707
01:20:06.080 --> 01:20:06.820
All right.

1708
01:20:07.220 --> 01:20:13.300
At 18 minutes, 23 seconds, Kevin is at his desk when Gabe starts his cookie monster impression.

1709
01:20:13.300 --> 01:20:20.220
And then at 18 minutes, 28 seconds, Kevin is now standing at Angela's desk as he starts

